+# Our compiled kernels in this directory: sources and exact build lines (ruj)
+
+Every cubin of ours that this image ships sits next to its CUDA source. Each one rebuilds **byte for byte** from that
+source with nvcc 13.4 (`Cuda compilation tools, release 13.4, V13.4.92`, `Build cuda_13.4.r13.4/compiler.38855100_0`),
+run in this directory:
+
+| cubin | source | build line | md5 of the cubin | used by |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `skx6.cubin` | `skx6.cu` | `nvcc -arch=sm_120a -O3 -cubin -Xptxas -v -o skx6.cubin skx6.cu` | `55a57eae00610aee283cefdccf6ccb08` | `mx.py` (MX two-class GEMM of the mixed 128 -> 192 graphs) |
+| `skx6t.cubin` | `skx6t.cu` | `nvcc -arch=sm_120a -O3 -cubin -Xptxas -v -o skx6t.cubin skx6t.cu` | `23ef7c9cd4485022635a2440a5f5093d` | `mx.py` with `S1ENG_SKX6T` (skx6 without its padded tail work) |
+| `kf.cubin` | `kf.cu` | `nvcc -O3 -arch=sm_120a -cubin -Xptxas -v -o kf.cubin kf.cu` | `c539fe299fca6eafc2251051a8f0d5a2` | `kf.py` (KF in-CTA split-K GEMM) |
+| `rn.cubin` | `rn.cu` | `nvcc -cubin -arch=sm_120a -O3 -fmad=false -Xptxas -v -o rn.cubin rn.cu` | `2e188b083929bbf17d0b047ec6f6c14a` | `rn.py` (RN norms; off in this image: `S1ENG_RN=0`) |
+
+* `-Xptxas -v` only prints the register use, but ptxas writes its own command line into the cubin's
+  `.note.nv.tkinfo` section. Without the flag the machine code is the same (`cuobjdump -sass` identical) and the
+  note differs, so the md5 differs. The older build notes (the `rn.cu` header, the kf lever notes) omit the flag.
+* Check: `md5sum *.cubin` after the build lines above, or compare `cuobjdump -sass` output.
+* The other cubins in this directory are not ours (rgh / kai): `ngemm5*`, `ngemm9*`, `ngr`, `ffs`, `kkt2n`, `onorm`,
+  `pron`, `xa`. `ngemm5.cubin` rebuilds from `ngemm5.cu` with `nvcc -arch=sm_120a -O3 -cubin -o ngemm5.cubin ngemm5.cu`
+  (md5 `4e6e162613b9e0261968bf7f8fb41402`).
